Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" State the objective:", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"51ab88a5-1e58-4803-a80d-d59c13bcf811"],

Cell["\<\
 Our objective is to find a simple, approximate description of the dynamic \
behavior of the spring-mass system.  No emphasis at this point is placed on \
secondary physical behaviors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e47dd428-f049-4e87-b086-31ba19ec2204"],

Cell[" Understand the problem:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6bc5bc0-9e96-4fe7-9dd3-0791c3c327ab"],

Cell["\<\
 Experiments and study are required before the modeling process can begin.
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"875389ad-93c4-440f-ae04-fc6670d01996"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Simplify the problem:", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ebaf19c2-d6ce-493a-abd7-66d4b4829783"],

Cell["\<\
 Every increase in detail (unless absolutely required to achieve our \
objective) increases the complexity, computation, difficulty, and cost of the \
model.

 Assumptions:
 
 No friction
 No viscous damping
 No spring hysteresis
 Spring linearity
 Massless spring
 Point mass
 No other forces
 Etc. etc.
 \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c91eaebf-04da-4b25-976b-fa373ab8de0a"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Categorize the problem:    Mechanical vs. Electrical \
vs. Chemical vs. Biological vs. Economic vs. Social vs. Etc. Etc.", \
"Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"8e2e97c9-5a6a-439d-8a16-\
40c112f1de12"],

Cell["\<\
  The problem can be best modeled as a mechanical problem
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f106d6b-9aaf-4f5d-914b-86d28e072807"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Mechanical problem:       Deterministic vs. \
probabilistic", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"95430b2b-2ab5-\
4872-ad51-a68aed9fa8d7"],

Cell["\<\
 The simple dynamics of the problem should yield effectively to a \
deterministic approach using Newton's laws of motion.
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d974c5bf-6609-468b-93e2-e8158f860081"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Mechanical problem:       Dynamic vs. non-dynamic", \
"Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"09dd5728-98f4-49c0-ac93-\
773abbb95b16"],

Cell["\<\
Our objectives clearly demand a dynamic solution (i.e. time is one of the \
independent variables).
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11bcc363-a82f-466b-a411-8c362488d165"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Mechanical problem:       Continuous vs. discrete", \
"Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6baac5f9-257a-4733-8e2b-\
6c5774cd8b33"],

Cell["\<\
 If Newton's laws of motion are used in their natural setting, then the \
obvious choice would be a continuous formulation (i.e. ODE or PDE) vs. a \
discrete formulation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cdfd5d4f-520b-472d-9396-24e386caab64"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Mechanical problem:       3-dimensional, \
2-dimensional, 1-dimensional, 0-dimensional  ", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",Exp\
ressionUUID->"0e624ce7-2f5e-41c1-8956-835a0df0a28c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" 3-Dimensional:       Advantages vs. disadvantages", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"7cb8eded-9b77-42fe-93d4-b9489dae4c10"],

Cell["\<\
 Formulation:  Requires a description of the system parameters spread over \
three space dimensions

 Advantages:  Possibility of increased accuracy

 Disadvantages:  Requires massive computation, requires increased physical \
understanding, requires greater care in formulation, etc. etc.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38630eb8-430c-4699-9b9a-70a113324bf0"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" 2-Dimensional:       Advantages vs. disadvantages", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"0b3b1927-61f0-4605-abe9-e4d4cae02b59"],

Cell["\<\
 Formulation: Requires a description of the system parameters spread over  \
two  space dimensions
 
 Advantages:\tPossibility of increased accuracy

 Disadvantages:   Loss of accuracy associated with mechanical behavior in the \
third dimension. 
                             Requires extensive computation, requires \
increased physical understanding, requires greater care in formulation, etc. \
etc.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"536aa707-1192-4cd8-987f-61360694f6b7"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" 1-Dimensional:       Advantages vs. disadvantages", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"535117a8-b4d1-4877-a038-fcf778acf713"],

Cell["\<\
 Formulation: Requires a description of the system parameters spread over one \
space dimension
 
 Advantages:\t Requires only moderate computation and moderate physical \
understanding

 Disadvantages:   Loss of accuracy associated with mechanical behavior in the \
second and third dimensions. 
                             Requires greater care in the formulation, etc. \
etc.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4867bd6d-fae0-464e-a89c-5692664f574a"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" 0-Dimensional:       Advantages vs. disadvantages", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"601e043e-cd22-4c98-b420-37d1aa9097f5"],

Cell["\<\
 Formulation: Requires a description of the system parameters at fixed \
locations (or a few \"point\" objects with movable locations) in space
 
 Advantages:\t Requires little computation and moderate physical \
understanding (i.e. this procedure only works for the simplest of problems)

 Disadvantages:   Loss of accuracy associated with mechanical behavior in the \
first, second and third dimensions. 
                             Requires even greater care in the formulation, \
etc. etc.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"804d54a2-1127-40f3-92e9-7c6570c0ad7d"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Our choice:", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"bd6f3330-eb10-4fec-9541-fd2b8323927b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To accomplish our objective of simplicity, treating our mass as a point \
mass and our assumption of no other physical characteristics, it seems \
reasonable to model the problem as a ",
 StyleBox["0-dimensional",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " problem.  \nThus, the only independent variable in the model will be time.\
\n"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"da587296-83a0-495b-8d73-5d2baef64b2e"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" List the dependent variables:", "Subtitle"]], \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9287ea44-2e6c-4ce4-a329-2fa493b6973f"],

Cell["\<\
 The important dependent variable would be position:   x[t], because velocity \
and acceleration can be directly calculated from the position information \
(i.e. x'[t] and x''[t]).
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a8c0914-6303-4d49-bd0e-7d1380c33cfb"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" List the independent variables:", "Subtitle"]], \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d23993a4-76ef-4637-bf65-0cbe31c27eff"],

Cell["\<\
 Important independent variables:          mass, spring constant

 Unimportant independent variables:     friction, viscous damping, mass of \
the spring, spring hysteresis, shape--size--surface--etc. of the mass etc. etc.
 \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"961faae6-a57a-49c9-96b8-711b0fdea068"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Model formulation:        Use existing procedure, or \
create a new procedure ", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->\
"9f37ee28-db05-4db1-a829-73c927c5e0c3"],

Cell["\<\
 The modeling objectives should be met by using existing procedures (i.e. \
Newton's laws of motion).  
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01db7ba0-f592-4b29-8c93-c36271579d9c"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Model formulation:        Generate a model", \
"Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2e6c4c3f-77e0-4d24-8af1-\
8e8ad7e1039b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " Under our assumptions: ",
 StyleBox[" \n\n\t\tThe model becomes:    m x'' = -kx\n", "Subsubsection"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982779338334*^9, 
  3.3982779362883997`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef146309-2c1a-4a92-889d-\
1463eadb05ce"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Solve the model:", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"ed6b59a1-a40e-46f1-899f-8aad15761e3f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sol1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"m", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "==", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "k"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "t"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982894193384*^9, 3.3982894194914*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[104]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c5a02e8e-0abe-4578-8493-10e96d38da40"],

Cell["\<\
It is possible to explicitly extract the formula for the solution from the \
replacement rule by using the following procedure: 
\tremove the outer list brackets:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d971543c-fed8-45c6-85b0-6627683f7438"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sol1", "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a5638417-f3da-\
45b3-a162-006e8050462c"],

Cell["\tremove the next list brackets:\[LineSeparator]", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3982773276354*^9},ExpressionUUID->"868f9ace-72dc-4c7c-b325-e143aa400c07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sol1", "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"77023e18-\
af39-45cb-8fc5-7b2bc0af5cd0"],

Cell["\<\
\t extract the second part (i.e. formula) from the replacement rule:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e4365e2-9d09-4e86-beae-27274a0e9f53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sol2", "=", 
  RowBox[{"sol1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID\
->"85508e04-fcc0-421e-ae49-f5070a7c1065"],

Cell["\<\
 However, the above procedure is not the recommended procedure for extracting \
a solution from a replacement rule.

The preferred method is to use replacement rules:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982774088194*^9, 
  3.3982774420973997`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f685bb6e-6ebe-4976-8f2f-\
26dd0d9ecf3e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "/.", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "sol1", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982773680704*^9, 3.3982773926354*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[105]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ae922e69-8cf2-490d-bc19-0bd2b9441c14"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Analyze the model's predictions:", "Subtitle"]], \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1a8a32a2-a117-472d-a404-7b7a6306c0b5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 " Examine the influence of stiffer springs:  i.e. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"k", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ",", "2", ",", "5", ",", "10"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"1334805f-6792-48b6-abc5-b0824bdede9e"]
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3982774806963997`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b9a051d0-4d3f-4984-b8f9-\
481d08b81487"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"sol3", "=", 
  RowBox[{"sol2", " ", "/.", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"C", "[", "1", "]"}], "\[Rule]", " ", "0"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"C", "[", "2", "]"}], "\[Rule]", " ", "1"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"m", "\[Rule]", " ", "1"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"k", "\[Rule]", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
